.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.br
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount
function reads the contents of the file pointed to by
.BR file
and counts the number of lines, words, and characters.

The calculated values are stored in the variables pointed to by
.BR lines ,
.BR words ,
and
.BR chars .

A word is identified as a sequence of characters separated by spaces,
newlines, or tab characters.

The function returns 0 when the operation is successful. It returns -1
if any of the input pointers is NULL.

